## Publication-gate remediation, round two (operator-directed, 2026-08-19)

The gate reported 121 blockers after automated remediation. The operator's
assistant rebuilt the claim lineage and evidence wiring directly; the gate now
passes with zero errors and zero warnings at 5,852 reader-facing words.

**Factual correction found during verification.** The module-move date was
wrong throughout the draft: the International Airport Review article (fetched
2026-08-19) was published August 12, 2025 and reports completion August 8,
2025 — not August 2026 as the opening, the release-for-fabrication section,
and the register table stated. All three corrected; footnote [^1] now carries
the verified date. Two research records had propagated the wrong year; the
correctly dated records are now the cited support.

**Lineage rebuilt.** 61 retained records, one per footnote, claims taken as
contiguous spans of the marked sentences, validated against the gate's own
citation-identification and evidence-support functions before writing.

**Evidence ledger supplemented (33 records, operator-approved).** The
Council's derived figures — schedule restructuring math, cost estimates, CPE
comparisons — were never recorded as ledger evidence, so their footnotes could
not trace. Each supplemental record quotes a byte-verbatim passage from the
run's own archived briefs, quantitative analysis, or strategist draft
(hard-asserted against the file before writing), is labeled
`council-analysis` with `source_path` provenance, and is never marked primary.
Footnotes over derived figures now say so explicitly.

**Primary-source checks.** `primary_source_checked` set true only where the
verified-claims table above documents the check, or the source was fetched
directly on 2026-08-19 (module-move article; IATA CUPPS page), or the figure
is council-derived and its excerpt was verified against the archived artifact.
Each record's verification note states which.

**Mechanical.** Footnotes renumbered into first-use order (42 labels moved);
29 sentences with numbers or attribution language received their governing
footnote marker or were reworded to remove incidental digits; rhetorical
year references (2043, 2035) de-digited where no factual claim was made.
